WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.173
Allow 4 minutes.

00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:09.285
Alignment means the objective names the intended performance, practice prepares learners for it, and assessment elicits evidence of it.

00:00:09.525 --> 00:00:16.523
Carnegie Mellon’s alignment guidance illustrates why recall-only tests do not establish an analytical objective.

00:00:17.213 --> 00:00:27.408
Worked example: objective “Judge an escalation proposal against impact, staffing, and response-time criteria.” Practice: compare two sample proposals,

00:00:27.408 --> 00:00:31.719
see a worked critique, then judge a third using those criteria.

00:00:31.959 --> 00:00:36.354
Assessment: select the strongest judgment of a new proposal and its reason.

00:00:36.594 --> 00:00:45.298
This selected-response assessment samples judgment; an independently written critique would provide additional evidence of the learner’s reasoning.

00:00:45.988 --> 00:00:53.967
Misaligned version: the same objective, followed only by a slide defining escalation and a quiz asking for the definition.

00:00:54.207 --> 00:00:56.895
The problem is not that definitions are useless.

00:00:57.135 --> 00:00:59.097
They may be necessary preparation.

00:00:59.337 --> 00:01:03.327
The problem is that the promised performance is never practiced or assessed.

00:01:04.017 --> 00:01:10.566
If the objective is Create, choosing somebody else’s plan is insufficient evidence of original production.

00:01:10.806 --> 00:01:15.542
Ask the learner to produce an artifact and assess it against transparent criteria.

00:01:15.782 --> 00:01:25.467
Do not claim that the multiple-choice assessment in this sample verifies creation skill; its objectives deliberately focus on classification and selection.

00:01:26.157 --> 00:01:27.245
Now it's your turn.

00:01:27.485 --> 00:01:30.643
Your objective requires producing a new onboarding plan.

00:01:30.883 --> 00:01:34.147
The test asks learners to pick the best of three finished plans.

00:01:34.387 --> 00:01:35.752
What is the best revision?

00:01:35.992 --> 00:01:39.107
Pause the video and make your choice in the activity below.

